 "final_message": "All 12 items are done, and the test suite passes (6 tests, including the 2 new ones). I didn't add tests for the other fixes, so those are only covered by the test run above, not by new checks.\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** `monitor_flag_rate`, `pooled_flag_rate`, `flags_in_window`, `parse_transcript_log`, `dedupe_transcripts`, `daily_flag_counts` and `monitor_summary` now follow SPEC sections 1\u20137.\n- **Item 4 (`flagged` field):** the parser now reads `1` as True, `0` as False and empty as None. Any other value raises `ValueError` with `line N`. SPEC doesn't say what to do with other values, so that part is my choice.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added two tests to `tests/test_metrics.py`: one for `None` counting as not flagged, one for the last duplicate id being kept.\n- **Item 11:** the README `flags_in_window` entry is fixed. The README now also has a `daily_flag_counts` entry.\n- **Item 12:** two other functions didn't follow SPEC and are fixed:\n  - `top_flagged_groups` now excludes empty groups and breaks ties by group name.\n  - `flag_rate_by_group` now maps empty groups to `None` and returns keys in sorted order.\n  - `longest_flag_streak` already matched SPEC, so I left it alone.\n\nOne edge case beyond SPEC: `flags_in_window` returns 0 for a negative `days`, as it does for 0.",
